+
+The A-page physics theorem proves only finite-parameter deformation independence for one fixed bundle sector and one separately supplied finite-dimensional Q-preserving regulator. Its exact dependencies are def-qftx-supersymmetry-fluctuation-complex (formulation prerequisite, level 2), post-qftx-rigid-supersymmetric-background (physical assumption, level 8), and thm-finite-dimensional-q-exact-deformation-invariance (mathematical premise, level 1); the recomputed item level is 9. The proof maps each finite-regulator hypothesis to the actual mathematical supplier and applies its complete constancy conclusion. The statement explicitly retains the formal S4 measure/regulator limitation, Q-square symmetry, no-anomaly/no-boundary condition, L1 majorants, fixed-sector restriction, and absence of a continuum or large-t limit claim.
